There is no need to reboot. Use the swapon -s command to check
current swapon size and locations. Amend the /etc/fstab file as
required, adding unused partitions as swap2 or swap 3, then run
swapon -a to "mount" all the swap partitions in fstab. Use swapon -s
again to check.
