	Of course, releasing existing swap space is not so easy.  I
upgraded the memory on my 500/500 from 256 MB to 512 MB and so wanted
to increase the swap from the 638 MB already configured.  I cleared a
2 GB partition (overkill, but it was the smallest empty partition.
Any way to repartition part of a disk?) and added that to the swap as
indicated above.

	However, I wanted my 638 MB back since 2 GB was plenty for
swap.  To do this I had to change the disklabel and then use fdisk to
put a ufs filesystem on the old swap partition.  I also had to change
the default swap entries in /etc/rc.config.


