M. Cao wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> The filesystem on my Digital Unix machine is Advfs, and rdump does not
> support Advfs.
> 
> Can you tell me how to backup my system to the remote tape drive ?

This was discussed some time ago.

Ther are two ways:

1. Create clones on target machine.
   Mount them via NFS on tape machine.
   Backup using vdump.

2. Enable rsh (/etc/hosts.equiv, .rhosts)
   Create clones on TARGET_HOST
   from tape machine: rsh TARGET_HOST -l root "vdump -f - /clones/root"
| dd -of /dev/nrmt0h
   (it's been a while and I could be wrong about syntax)

Nix.




