I have done some attempts with setld and finally decided, that .tar.gz and
my own installation script is a better solution. The main reason is, that
setld kit can not be built and installed without root privilege. In
particular you can not place kit building code into product makefiles (I
don't compile on root, do you?) and can not install patches without root
priv even if an application is installed on dedicated account (as it is in
my case). As the main products we utilize (Oracle, Tuxedo, JAM) are not put
into setld kits, the dependence checking mechanism is also worthless for me
(I check software versions and existance using shell script checking
existence of some crucial files).

Could anyone share opinions of how to distribute software packages on DU?





