Hi.

We are working with SAP R/3 and Digital AlphaServer 8400/8200 + DU4.0D, and
right now we haven't clustering implementd, but is really necessary.

SAP architecture is a tipical central host architecture (not a really
client/server) and you always need a Central Dabatabase Server. You can grow
adding Aplications servers to release CPU time and Spool services of the
Database Server. It means that you have a critical point in your installation
that must be solved: failover of your Database server.

We have implemented RAID 0+1 system on disk, double redundant FDDI/Ethernet
cards (FDDI-DAS), double power supply, and so on, but if server crashes the
system will be down.

This is the main reason because we're planing to implement DECSafe / Clustering
techniques.

I think that the decision depends of the critical level that a crash may
represent for your company.

Hope it helps.

Xavi Roig.
SAP R/3 administrator
